Third-party code
----------------
Pantheon links Foundry (https://git.teamide.dev/David/Foundry.git), which is
under the same AGPL-3.0 terms and the same copyright holder.

src/accel/tt/pn_tt_device.c uses the ARC telemetry tag numbers and names
defined by the TelemetryTag enumeration of tt-umd
(https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-umd), (c) 2025 Tenstorrent Inc.,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Only those numbers and names
are used; no tt-umd source code is included. A copy of the Apache License 2.0
is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

lib/monocypher/ is Monocypher 4.0.3 (https://monocypher.org/), used by
Pantheon Local to verify catalog signatures (Ed25519, minisign format).
Copyright (c) 2017-2023 Loup Vaillant, (c) 2017-2019 Michael Savage,
(c) 2017-2023 Fabio Scotoni. Dual-licensed CC0-1.0 OR BSD-2-Clause; Pantheon
uses it under BSD-2-Clause. The full license text, with the copyright notices
that binary distributions must reproduce, is in lib/monocypher/LICENSE.
Provenance (version, tarball sha256) is in lib/monocypher/README.md.

src/serve/tool_calling.c contains short tool-prompt fragments copied verbatim
from model chat templates, so the prompt matches the model's own rendering:
the Qwen tools block (Qwen3-Coder / Qwen3.5 family chat_template, Qwen team,
Alibaba Cloud) and the MiniCPM5 tools block (openbmb/MiniCPM5 chat_template,
OpenBMB). Both model repositories are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

tests/bonsai_phase3b/mb_q2_0_matvec.c (a private diagnostic, not part of the
public release) transcribes the Q2_0/Q8_0 dot-product and fp16 conversion
math of ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml, via the PrismML llama.cpp
fork), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors, MIT License.

tools/dflash_accept.py (not part of the public release) is a modified NumPy
port of the DFlash drafter forward pass and greedy loop in dflash/model.py of
z-lab/dflash (https://github.com/z-lab/dflash), Copyright (c) 2026 Z Lab,
MIT License.

evals/gpqa/gpqa_dataset.py uses the QUERY_TEMPLATE_MULTICHOICE prompt from
OpenAI simple-evals (https://github.com/openai/simple-evals),
Copyright (c) 2024 OpenAI, MIT License.

